{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-quantum-gap-collapse","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:quantum-gap-collapse","kind":"theorem","title":"Collapse of the quantum gap","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-limit-functor","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-reeb-derivation"],"tags":["quantum-gap","classical-limit","collapse","braiding-trivialization"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.quantum_gap_collapse","text":"quantum-gap-collapse.md","leanSource":"quantum-gap-collapse.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:quantum-gap-collapse\"></a><p>Under the classical limit functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}</code>, the following degenerations occur simultaneously:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Planck constant</strong>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q = 1 - q^{-1} \\to 0</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-differential</strong>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q \\to d</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Braiding</strong>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}_q</code> degenerates to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}_1</code>, as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R(q) \\to \\mathrm{id} \\otimes \\mathrm{id}</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Reeb period</strong>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega_q \\to \\infty</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Formally, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}</code> sends <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_q</code> to a commutative Hopf algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_1 = \\mathcal{O}(\\mathcal{B}_{\\mathrm{cl}})</code>, the coordinate ring of the classical Bring's curve. The self-duality <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_q \\simeq \\omega_{A_q}^\\bullet</code> descends to classical Serre duality.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"21.4.3","page":"b/thm-quantum-gap-collapse","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":79},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Core.AlgebraicSubstrate.quantum_gap_collapse","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
